      "pad_after": 0.35,
      "min_duration": 5.0,
      "lines": [
        "The flame is over a thousand degrees. The plastic melts at one twenty. But it never gets close."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "equation",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "min_duration": 6.0,
      "lines": [
        "Heat flow is k, delta T, over d. The film is point zero three millimeters thin, so heat shoots straight through into the water."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ceiling",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.4,
      "min_duration": 5.5,
      "lines": [
        "And water can't pass a hundred degrees. Once it boils, every extra joule becomes steam, not hotter plastic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "punch",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.45,
      "min_duration": 4.2,
      "lines": [
        "So the plastic sits at a hundred. Twenty below melting. It cannot melt."
